    "created_at": "2024-10-09T16:53:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-09T16:53:34Z",
    "body": "This sounds reasonable, and likely to be web compatible, at least to me. It seems very corner-case to create a document, put a popover in it, and call `showPopover()` expecting things to happen. There's always the chance that there's a use case, but I can't think of one. I suppose it's possible that people do that and then move those elements to a rendered document and expect things to be \"still open\", but that's not what happens today, other than an open non-modal dialog because of the `open` attribute.\r\n\r\nI'd be relatively happy to take the risk of compat shipping this change, if there's consensus.",
